DLE_HBM_MIB=1024\\nOUTPUT_ROOT=\\\"${REPO_ROOT}/benchmark_results/serving_suite\\\"\\nDRY_RUN=0\\nCHECK_ONLY=0\\nBREAKDOWN=0\\nKV_BYTE_METRICS=0\\nCD3_CPU_PROFILE=0\\nDATASET_PATH=\\\"\\\"\\nSMOKE=0\\n\\nusage() {\\n  cat <<'EOF'\\nUsage: scripts/serving/run_performance_suite.sh [options]\\n\\nWith --kv-byte-metrics, KV byte counts and compression/transfer ratios are\\nsaved under each cell's kv_metrics directory and linked from summary.tsv.\\n--breakdown also records diagnostic GPU timing. The byte counts cover all\\nserver forwards, not the client's trimmed request cohort.\\n\\nRuns isolated llama70b serving experiments. Every combination of KV mode,\\nchunk size, request rate, and repeat gets a fresh server process.\\n\\nOptions:\\n  --codecs LIST                 p4flat,cd3 (default: p4flat,cd3)\\n  --modes LIST                  raw,kvcomp (default: raw,kvcomp)\\n  --cd3-base-rows LIST          CD3 base-sharing rows: 1,16,32,64\\n                                (default: 16; applies only to CD3 cells)\\n  --cd3-kv-storage MODE         KV mode: csr (append/serial) or hybrid (pipeline; default)\\n  --chunks LIST                 Comma-separated max_num_batched_tokens\\n                                (default: 2048,4096,8192)\\n  --request-rates LIST          Comma-separated rates; each gets a fresh server\\n                                (default: 1.2)\\n  --repeats N                   Full matrix repetitions (default: 1)\\n  --max-num-seqs N              vLLM max_num_seqs (default: 128)\\n  --num-prompts N               Client requests to send (default: 1200)\\n  --skip-first-n-requests N     Leading requests excluded from metrics\\n                                (default: 100)\\n  --skip-last-n-requests N      Trailing requests excluded from metrics\\n                                (default: 100)\\n  --dedicated-kv-blocks N       Logical dedicated KV blocks (default: 2432)\\n  --weight-huge-pages N         16-GiB weight huge pages (default: 14)\\n  --weight-buffers N            Weight staging buffers (default: 2)\\n  --numa-node N                 NUMA node for the server (default: 0)\\n  --gpu-index N                 CUDA/nvidia-smi GPU index (default: 0)\\n  --startup-timeout SEC         Server readiness timeout (default: 900)\\n  --shutdown-timeout SEC        Graceful shutdown timeout (default: 120)\\n  --cleanup-timeout SEC         Clean-state boundary timeout (default: 180)\\n  --max-idle-hbm-mib N          Maximum HBM considered idle (default: 1024)\\n  --output-root PATH            Suite output root\\n  --stop-after-request N        Stop after send-order requests 1..N have all\\n                                completed. Later requests keep arriving until\\n                                then and are cancelled at the boundary. Use\\n                                1100 to preserve the default 1200/100/100\\n                                measurement window; 0 waits for all (default)\\n  --breakdown                   Record KV byte counters and diagnostic timing\\n                                for every server forward, with layer/component interval,\\n                                wait and pipeline-state CSVs (client perf is invalid)\\n  --kv-byte-metrics             Record per-forward KV byte counters without\\n                                diagnostic GPU timing; client perf remains valid\\n  --cd3-cpu-profile             Record CD3 KV CPU phase timing in kv_metrics\\n                                (diagnostic; client perf is invalid)\\n  --dataset-path PATH           Azure conversation CSV for client requests\\n                                (default: vLLM's Azure conversation trace)\\n  --smoke                       Run two requests without percentile trimming;\\n                                validates startup and request handling only\\n  --check-only                  Validate files, dependencies, and clean state\\n  --dry-run                     Print the complete matrix and commands\\n  -h, --help 